      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the repacking goes (see my comment on the commit message), this hint handling would need to go back too, at least for anonymous VMAs. Otherwise a hint at another slice would move the PTEs without fixing their slices. Before this patch, such a hint made the search start from its 16KB window and keep the source slice. A hint isn\u0027t binding, so that\u0027s still valid, and `mremap_hint_p3s` in aosp/4367986 would then expect the slice-preserving address rather than the hint.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "e18c1fcd04a4a8bb9444482f9172d48ac7eaf018",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ae47521_6f015988",
        "filename": "mm/mremap.c",
        "patchSetId": 25
      },
      "lineNbr": 1778,
      "author": {
        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T18:25:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think these alignment changes (here, for `vrm-\u003enew_addr`, and for the lengths in `do_mremap()`) aren\u0027t needed. `mm/mremap.c` includes `\u003clinux/p3s_user_pages.h\u003e`, so on arm64 `__offset_in_page_log()`, `__offset_in_page()` and `__PAGE_ALIGN()` already use the 4KB process page in a 4KB process.\n\nThey also drop ACK\u0027s x86_64 page size emulation from `d687e7b29d66` (`\"ANDROID: 16K: mremap: __PAGE_ALIGN addr and len`\"), since `mm_pte_size()` is the 4KB kernel page there. Would it be OK to keep the original lines?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "e18c1fcd04a4a8bb9444482f9172d48ac7eaf018",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
