      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T18:25:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that file and shmem VMAs need the source slice here once `mremap()` can move them to another slice, so my earlier comment on aosp/4367608 no longer applies.\n\nWould you mind moving the choice into a helper next to `vma_slice_offset()` in `include/linux/p3s/vma.h`, so that `copy_vma()` keeps one-line hooks? Something like:\n\n```\n\tunsigned short slice_off \u003d vma_mremap_slice_off(vma, old_addr, addr);\n\t...\n\tvmg_set_slice_off(\u0026vmg, slice_off);\n```\n\nThe helper would carry the comment. It would return `vma_slice_offset(vma, old_addr)` for VMAs with `vm_file` or `vm_ops`, and `vma_slice_offset(vma, addr)` otherwise. For anonymous VMAs that\u0027s the value `VMG_VMA_STATE()` already set, so the second line changes nothing for them.",
      "isAi": true,
